Title: The Last Signal

INT. LISTENING STATION - NIGHT

Radio static. MARA VALE (40s) sits at the console, headphones half on.

ANNOUNCER (V.O.)
This is the final scheduled broadcast from Earth. Thank you for listening.

Mara turns the receiver's dial until the carrier tone thins to nothing.

MARA
(to herself)
That's it, then.

INT. LISTENING STATION - NIGHT

The speaker stack wakes, one channel at a time.

Mara leaves the console and stops two steps short of the stack.

SPEAKER STACK (V.O.)
That's it, then.

MARA
I never sent that.

The stack repeats it, quieter. She does not move.
